    "created_at": "2016-09-27T17:33:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-27T17:33:14Z",
    "body": "I don't care for for the key event example @domenic  provided there. At least for keyboard events we want to take advantage of threaded scrolling. But having javascript filter every key event prevents that so a filter on the registered event listener is best for the UA for some apps that only care about certain keys; like 'Enter'. Then PageUp/PageDown can be accelerated and not dispatch javascript at all. But +1 for Observables.\n",
