    "created_at": "2016-10-14T03:19:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-14T03:19:54Z",
    "body": "You can't make that assumption, though, can you? JavaScript runtime performance and DOM standards conformity aren't inherently linked. And it still only addresses half of what I'm saying. Weak hardware isn't going to like additional allocations regardless of standards conformity.\n",
