    "updated_at": "2017-02-01T23:45:31Z",
    "body": "Although it only bears tangential relevance, Rust's [`futures` library](https://docs.rs/futures) is 1. 100% pull-based, and 2. requires you to use `stream.for_each` and connect the resulting future to an event loop to be able to react to changes. JS has a native event loop and is much more idiomatically push-based, which makes that kind of model much more awkward.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
