    "updated_at": "2017-02-01T23:51:26Z",
    "body": "I don't think this is a problem for this proposal. This Promise-based API would behave like a listener added with `once` specified. So it is a one-off thing. If you need to continuously monitor an event like `mousemove`, it makes no sense to use it. It is mostly for replacing the structure of\r\n```js\r\nelem.addEventListener(type, function handler() {\r\n  elem.removeEventListener(type, handler);\r\n  doSomething();\r\n});\r\n```\r\nor the new syntax\r\n```js\r\nelem.addEventListener(type, function() {\r\n  doSomething();\r\n}, {once: true});\r\n```\r\nwith\r\n```js\r\nawait elem.on(type);\r\ndoSomething();\r\n```",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/dom/issues/comments/276821851/reactions",
