    "created_at": "2017-02-02T06:38:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-02-02T06:38:13Z",
    "body": "What makes that any different than what you can do already? It's fairly easy to pull into a utility function.\r\n\r\n```js\r\nfunction on(elem, type) {\r\n    return new Promise(resolve => {\r\n        elem.addEventListener(type, function listener(ev) {\r\n            this.removeEventListener(type, listener, false)\r\n            resolve(ev)\r\n        }, false)\r\n    })\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd given the new `once` option, I seriously doubt such a thing is worth it.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
